              will serve as a framework for investigating a range of imaginative
              phenomena of interest to aestheticians, including genre,
              imaginative blockage, and the range of conative states we take on
              in engaging with various fictions. But to tell this story about how
              the imagination interacts with various parts of the mind, I first
              need to tell the tale of what those parts are, and indeed what the
              imagination is such that it makes sense to talk about such
              interactions.}}

